nceIndex": 0, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "25. \"A person who performs two rakaats of salaat in seclusion, where nobody except Allah and His Angeks see him, receives a writ of deliverance from the fire of hell.\" 26. \"Grant of one prayer (wish) becomes due to a person from Allah after each fardh salaat performed by him.\" 27. \"Fire of Hell is forbidden and the Paradise becomes due to a person who performs his wudhu properly and says his salaat conscientiously, according to its regulations. \" 28. 29. 30. 31. 32. \"The Devil remains scared of a Muslim so long as he is particular about his salaat, but no sooner does he neglect it than the Devii gets a hold.upon him and aspires for success in seducing him. i'' \"Salaat at its early hours is the most excellent practice.\" \" Salaat is the offering of the pious.\" \"Salaat at its early hours is a practice most liked by Allah. \" \"At. dawn, some people go to the musjid and some to the market. Those going to the musjid are the flag-bearers of Imaan and those leaving for the market are the flag-bearers of the Devil. \" 333 \"The four rakaats before Zuhr have the same reward as the four rakaats of Tahajjud. \" 34. \"The four rakaats before Zuhr are counted equal (in reward) to the four rakaats of Tahajjud.\" 35. \"Mercy of Allah turns towards a person standing in salaat.\" 36. \"Salaat at the dead of night is most valued, but there are very few who do it. \" \"Jibra-eel (Alayhis salaam) came to me and said, 37. O, Muhammad (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam)! however long thou livest thou shalt die one day, and whoever, thou may love thou shalt depart from him one day. Surely, thou shalt receive the recompense of whatever (good or evil) thou dost. No", "rawOcrText": "28 Virtues of Salaat 25. \"A person who performs two rakaats of salaat in seclusion, where nobody except Allah and His Angeks see him, receives a writ of deliverance from the fire of hell.\" 26. • \"Grant of one prayer (wish) becomes due to a person from Allah after each fardh salaat per- formed by him.\" 27. \"Fire of Hell is forbidden and the Paradise be- comes due to a person who performs his wudhu properly and says his salaat conscientiously, according to its regulations. \" 28. 29. 30. 31. 32. \"The Devil remains scared of a Muslim so long as he is particular about his salaat, but no sooner does he neglect it than the Devii gets a hold .upon him and aspires for success in seducing him. i'' \"Salaat at its early hours is the most excellent practice.\" \" Salaat is the offering of the pious.\" \"Salaat at its early hours is a practice most liked by Allah. \" \"At. dawn, some people go to the musjid and some to the market. Those going to the musjid are the flag-bearers of Imaan and those leaving for the market are the flag-bearers of the Devil. \" 333 \"The four rakaats before Zuhr have the same reward as the four rakaats of Tahajjud. \" 34. \"The four rakaats before Zuhr are counted equal (in reward) to the four rakaats of Tahajjud.\" 35. \"Mercy of Allah turns towards a person standing in salaat.\" 36. \"Salaat at the dead of night is most valued, but there are very few who do it. \" \"Jibra-eel (Alayhis salaam) came to me and said, 37. O, Muhammad (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam)! how- ever long thou livest thou shalt die one day, and whoever, thou may love thou shalt depart from him one day. Surely, thou shalt receive the recom- pense of whatever (good or evil) thou dost. No", "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}], "pageNumber": 28}'::jsonb);
